1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,200
The load does 500 kW of useful work: P.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:07,000
Motors also need reactive power, Q.

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:11,900
Together they make apparent power S: 625 kVA.

4
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:17,800
Generator current follows S, not P. The power factor is 0.8.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,900
Current heats the windings. That is why generators are rated in kVA.

6
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:30,200
In the control room: watch kW and kVA. A low power factor means more current.

7
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:34,900
Then you may need the next generator sooner.

8
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:39,900
kW does the work. kVA heats the generator.
